  "source_review": {
    "review": "The sorted singular values define the entire consecutive above/tied threshold block. Finite cyclic selections have the stated exact counts and actual rank/orthonormal frames. Every selected projector has the actual first tail error. Equality residuals yield the exact take/tied mean identity, full-tie annihilation, and strict residual contraction for some candidate when positive. Arbitrary orthonormal frames implement their actual QQ\u1d40 span projector.",
    "limits": "Singular-direction conclusions range over Fin(min m l); positive threshold directions are covered. This is the matrix tie construction, with no complete tensor algorithm, RAM implementation or global complexity claim."
  },
